{"id": "EUVD-2026-76528", "enisaUuid": "6d80f8f7-b1dd-360d-8994-dc636cd70a87", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfs/ntfs3: fix info-leak on partial LZNT decompress in ni_read_frame()\n\nni_read_frame() decompresses an LZNT $DATA frame into the vmapped target\npages and then trusts decompress_lznt()'s return value:\n\n  unc_size = decompress_lznt(frame_ondisk, ondisk_size, frame_mem,\n                             frame_size);\n  if ((ssize_t)unc_size < 0)        err = unc_size;\n  else if (!unc_size || unc_size > frame_size)  err = -EINVAL;\n\ndecompress_lznt() stops as soon as the compressed stream is exhausted\n(e.g. a zero chunk header) and returns the number of bytes it actually\nwrote, which may be far less than frame_size. The bytes between unc_size\nand frame_size are never written. The only memset() that follows zeroes\nthe region beyond i_valid; when the frame lies entirely within the file's\nvalid size that memset() does not run, so the gap retains whatever was in\nthe just-vmapped pages. All pages are then marked uptodate and returned\nto userspace, disclosing uninitialized (recently-freed) kernel page\nmemory. A crafted compressed file whose stream decompresses to only a few\nbytes leaks the remainder of every frame on a plain read(2), which is\nenough to recover kernel pointers and defeat KASLR.\n\nZero the [unc_size, frame_size) tail immediately after a successful LZNT\ndecompress so the remainder reads back as zero.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:45:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:49:48", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7d60a4c49af4d5cb88aa7cbf998d0408bd415055", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cd40eee4923d104ebec9ac7513b971bc441e431d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/77d8efd04745cda23858546afdbd9d07b591758e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0f699ddb290a24b37e1bc9bf1e3c9dbccf564bea", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/376ee45659a4b943df672ad275c63da00655f929", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4a1b39b2e10eb8de86265e80cf2be4396bc1dce4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/35d1ea92c7d946e2ebdbe36cdb2c969c8704bebd"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89616", "GHSA-486v-9mj8-37c6"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.42, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0912eca7-993e-3c1d-aebd-32e2141e752e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "0f6a6614-2f89-323b-9dce-78a7627b5db1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4342306f0f0d5ff4315a204d315c1b51b914fca5 <0f699ddb290a24b37e1bc9bf1e3c9dbccf564bea"}, {"id": "1bde3477-0fd6-3014-bdb9-a1c7d87945a5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4342306f0f0d5ff4315a204d315c1b51b914fca5 <77d8efd04745cda23858546afdbd9d07b591758e"}, {"id": "21209a75-3b07-3e4f-80f4-e280a2042464", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4342306f0f0d5ff4315a204d315c1b51b914fca5 <35d1ea92c7d946e2ebdbe36cdb2c969c8704bebd"}, {"id": "3fbdd43c-6d3e-3bba-87fe-1eb34b7f924c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4342306f0f0d5ff4315a204d315c1b51b914fca5 <7d60a4c49af4d5cb88aa7cbf998d0408bd415055"}, {"id": "445671be-3005-38ad-b087-b3bc5c35d64c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "517ef70f-c3a9-3287-9a8d-cc37f2b2fa65", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "78e0633c-a9ca-3bdc-9bc3-9fa6b08b0140", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "80efc676-9c4b-362d-9fed-b73af330a46a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15"}, {"id": "a2bb8461-6905-3e85-8f1e-70ccc6669843", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name"